}

docs {
  ## Settle Ledger Balance — POST /expense/user/:userId/ledger/settle

  **Accounts (or Superuser) only.** Records a manual correction to an
  executive's outstanding Payable balance in one step — inserts a new
  advance-type row that's pre-approved and marked paid immediately, so it
  shows up in the transaction ledger as a single **Consolidation Adjustment**
  credit rather than a separate Advance Request + Payment Made pair.

  Use this to reconcile a balance directly (e.g. a cash settlement outside
  the normal expense-submission flow) rather than creating a new expense claim.

  ### Request body

  | Field   | Type   | Required | Notes                                  |
  |---------|--------|----------|-------------------------------------------|
  | amount  | number | yes      | must be a positive number                  |
  | comment | string | no       | free text, stored as the accounts_comment  |

  ### Response (200) — `data` object

  | Field      | Type | Notes                              |
  |------------|------|-------------------------------------|
  | expense_id | int  | the generated settlement row's id   |
}
